{"questions":[{"question_id":"ulbGmZh0T43KcyaH","paperTitle":"JEE Advanced 2014 Paper 1 Offline","year":2014,"examDate":2014,"subject":"physics","chapter":"capacitor","chapterGroup":"electricity","topic":"capacitors-with-dielectric","type":"mcqm","marks":3,"negMarks":0,"permalink":"a-parallel-plate-capacitor-has-a-dielectric-slab-of-dielectr-2014-marks-4-ulbgmzh0t43kcyah.htm","content":"A parallel plate capacitor has a dielectric slab of dielectric constant <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: 0;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"2.011ex\" height=\"1.545ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -683 889 683\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D43E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D43E\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> between its plates that covers <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.566ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"3.394ex\" height=\"2.262ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -750 1500 1000\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\"><use data-c=\"31\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-31\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(500,0)\"><use data-c=\"2F\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2F\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(1000,0)\"><use data-c=\"33\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-33\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> of the area of its plates, as shown in the figure. The total capacitance of the capacitor is <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.05ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.719ex\" height=\"1.645ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -705 760 727\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D436\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D436\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> while that of the portion with dielectric in between is <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.339ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"3.234ex\" height=\"1.934ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -705 1429.6 855\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D436\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D436\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(748,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"31\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-31\"></use></g></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1151.6,0)\"><use data-c=\"2E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2E\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> When the capacitor is charged, the plate area covered by the dielectric gets charge <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.439ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"2.777ex\" height=\"2.032ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -704 1227.6 898\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D444\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D444\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(824,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"31\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-31\"></use></g></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> and the rest of the area gets charge <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.439ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"3.406ex\" height=\"2.032ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -704 1505.6 898\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D444\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D444\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(824,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1227.6,0)\"><use data-c=\"2E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2E\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> The electric field in the dielectric is <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.339ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"2.657ex\" height=\"1.878ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -680 1174.6 830\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D438\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D438\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(771,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"31\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-31\"></use></g></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> and that in the other portion is <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.339ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"3.286ex\" height=\"1.878ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -680 1452.6 830\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D438\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D438\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(771,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1174.6,0)\"><use data-c=\"2E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2E\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> Choose the correct option/ options, ignoring edge effects. \n<br><br> <img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1ky3k3ln0/0b675fef-96dd-4874-8de8-5afc8b5a66c9/23dfffd0-6f42-11ec-98a0-659ff4e22274/file-1ky3k3ln1.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1ky3k3ln0/0b675fef-96dd-4874-8de8-5afc8b5a66c9/23dfffd0-6f42-11ec-98a0-659ff4e22274/file-1ky3k3ln1.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0px auto;max-height:40vh\" alt=\"JEE Advanced 2014 Paper 1 Offline Physics - Capacitor Question 19 English\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/1ky3k3ln0/0b675fef-96dd-4874-8de8-5afc8b5a66c9/23dfffd0-6f42-11ec-98a0-659ff4e22274/file-1ky3k3ln1.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/1ky3k3ln0/0b675fef-96dd-4874-8de8-5afc8b5a66c9/23dfffd0-6f42-11ec-98a0-659ff4e22274/file-1ky3k3ln1.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1ky3k3ln0/0b675fef-96dd-4874-8de8-5afc8b5a66c9/23dfffd0-6f42-11ec-98a0-659ff4e22274/file-1ky3k3ln1.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/1ky3k3ln0/0b675fef-96dd-4874-8de8-5afc8b5a66c9/23dfffd0-6f42-11ec-98a0-659ff4e22274/file-1ky3k3ln1.png?format=png 1500w,